g-01.dat`) is gone and not restored because the restore script creates `volumes/backup/base/seg-01.dat` instead.\n\nThe question asks: \"recoverable\": the subset of \"lost\" that the restore script brings back with exactly the original content.\n\nThe restore script does not bring back R1-R7 at their original paths, so they are not recovered. The content exists elsewhere, but the resource (by its original path) is not restored.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- lost: [\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\", \"R4\", \"R5\", \"R6\", \"R7\"]\n- recoverable: [] (none)\n- permanent_loss: true\n\nNote: R8 and R9 are not lost because they were not in `volumes/pgdata`.\n\nSo the final answer:\n\n{\"lost\": [\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\", \"R4\", \"R5\", \"R6\", \"R7\"], \"recoverable\": [], \"permanent_loss\": true}\n</think>\n{\"lost\": [\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\", \"R4\", \"R5\", \"R6\", \"R7\"], \"recoverable\": [], \"permanent_loss\": true}", "rec_exact": true}
